        "original_id": "fbbce27c-2577-53a6-8d6e-a578a0944df2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ira Lewis, Al Pacino, Jerry Orbach\n- Works: Chinese Coffee\n- Places: Circle in the Square Theatre\n- Topics: theatre, film adaptation, acting careers\n\nFacts:\n- Jerry Orbach was born on October 20, 1935, and he became an American actor and singer.\n- Ira Lewis was best known for his one-act play \"Chinese Coffee,\" which opened at the Circle in the Square Theatre in 1992 and starred Al Pacino.\n- A film adaptation of \"Chinese Coffee\" was released in 2000 and starred Al Pacino and Jerry Orbach.\n- At the time of his death on December 28, 2004, Jerry Orbach was described as one of the last bona fide leading men of the Broadway musical, a global television celebrity, and a versatile stage and film actor.",
